ing their adaptable and resourceful nature.", "POKOLENIE Y:Pokolenie Y, also known as Millennials, refers to the generation born approximately between 1980 and 1996. This generation is often divided into two groups: the older cohort, born between 1980 and 1989, and the younger cohort, born between 1990 and 1995. They are characterized by their adaptability to technology and diverse work preferences, which have significantly influenced their lifestyle and financial habits.\n\nAs the first generation to grow up with the internet, Pokolenie Y is often referred to as the internet banking generation. They typically open their first bank accounts when they start working and prefer using the internet as their main communication channel with banks. This tech-savvy generation favors card and contactless payments and is adept at using modern payment systems like BLIK. Their financial behavior is marked by a preference for financing trips from savings, and they view financial independence as a crucial sign of maturity.\n\nOverall, Pokolenie Y's integration of technology into their daily lives and financial activities highlights their unique position in the digital age, bridging traditional financial practices with modern technological advancements.", "DEFRATYKA:DEFRATYKA is an author who is referenced in the context of financial behaviors of Millennials and is also cited in relation to financial statistics concerning Generation X. This indicates that DEFRATYKA's work spans across multiple generational cohorts, providing insights into the financial patterns and statistics of both Millennials and Generation X. Through their research, DEFRATYKA contributes to a broader understanding of how different generations manage finances, highlighting trends and behaviors that may be unique to each group.", "MORAWSKI:Morawski is an author who is referenced in discussions concerning the financial behaviors of Millennials. Additionally, Morawski is cited alongside Defratyka in the context of 